Two subspecies are currently recognised by the Australian Plant Census:
Hakea salicifolia (Vent.) B.L.Burtt subsp. salicifolia that has leaves more than {{cvt|7|mm}} wide and grows on the coast and ranges from Springbrook, Queensland to Jervis Bay, New South Wales;
Hakea salicifolia subsp. angustifolia (A.A.Ham.) W.R.Barker that has leaves {{cvt|4–7|mm}} wide and grows near water courses between Hornsby and Helensburgh in the Sydney region.
